# Automation Standards

**Split in P4.** This file is the general tooling policy — what to reach for, in
what order, and what needs Lead approval. Two things moved out:

- the PA-E / MRQ / capture precondition rules are lookdev evidence policy and now
  live in [`lookdev-evidence-standards.mdc`](lookdev-evidence-standards.mdc);
- the "variables with no access" procedure now has a single canonical home in
  [`19-automation-gaps.mdc`](19-automation-gaps.mdc). **Do not restate it here.**

## Editor UI automation is the default

When we can drive the Unreal Editor UI automatically, that is the **default
method** — not a fallback. Prefer running the GUI automation script; treat
manual Editor steps as fallback only when GUI automation is unavailable (ref
images not captured, script not runnable here) or has failed.

Maintain ref images and scripts so the default path stays available. Patterns:
`docs/Automation/FULL_AUTOMATION_RESEARCH.md` §10.

## KNOWN_ERROR_LOG (Lead hard rule)

Along-the-way logging is required, but **always-on it is one line: Cause → Avoid.**
Detail belongs in [`docs/KNOWN_ERRORS.md`](../../docs/KNOWN_ERRORS.md), retrieved
on failure. Never paste episode narratives into agent profile memory or into an
always-apply rule. Cap new always-on gate additions; prefer a pointer to a
KNOWN_ERRORS section anchor (e.g. § PA-E DESKTOP prove misses).

## Fold corrections into the harness immediately

When the Lead corrects a **proven** miss (DESKTOP evidence, false PASS/FAIL),
fold it into the repo at once: a blocking gate, an assert threshold, or one row in
`PROVE_CRITERIA`. Not a long runbook, and not rediscovering the same rule in
chat next time. Prefer compact hard rules over verbose prose.

## The ladder

Work down this list. Do not skip rungs because a rung is slow.

1. **Docs-first** — read official Epic (or vendor) docs before inventing or
   hardening console commands, Editor Python APIs, MCP usage, or commandlets,
   unless the usage is already in repo policy. Match documented **parameter
   order**, **context**, and **output paths**; do not infer syntax from a failed
   prove.
2. **Proven-results first** — prioritise docs plus proven community/industry
   patterns for the same goal, before custom ladders, long waits, or novel
   stacks.
3. **Rung 1 — harden what exists** — UE/host built-ins and scripts already in the
   repo. Re-try after engine or tool updates.
4. **Research on dead-ends** — after rung-1 hardening fails *with evidence*, run
   **one** proactive public research pass (forums, issues, known bugs) and log
   it in the AUTOMATION_GAPS research log, *before* recommending escalation or
   asking the Lead an open-ended question.
5. **Rung 2 — third-party tools** — only after **`APPROVE TOOL SCOUT <name>`**.
   No auto-install.
6. **Rung 3 — net-new stacks** — only after **`APPROVE TOOL BUILD <name>`**. No
   unprompted frameworks.

Capture/MRQ/HighResShot/NirCmd/OBS are **examples** of this ladder
(`docs/Automation/CAPTURE_REDUNDANCY.md` § Shotlist instance), not the limit of
its scope.

